  "title": "Erdős Problem #774",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "We call $A\\subset \\mathbb{N}$ dissociated if $\\sum_{n\\in X}n\neq \\sum_{m\\in Y}m$ for all finite $X,Y\\subset A$ with $X\neq Y$.\nLet $A\\subset \\mathbb{N}$ be an infinite set. We call $A$ proportionately dissociated if every finite $B\\subset A$ contains a dissociated set of size $\\gg \\lvert B\\rvert$.\nIs every proportionately dissociated set the union of a finite number of dissociated sets?",
